# K03 NS-ROLES-1b (Codex K03-S5-ALIAS-VISIBILITY-20261007-07 Q1, K03-NS-ROLES-NEXT-20261007-09; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md
# :666, :722): for absent b, `b: tick` with tick a method binds b to tick's whole occurrence -- no wrapper, nothing
# runs at the binding; `b: args` and `b(args)` call tick, with its signature, on the occurrence b holds.
# The occurrence b holds is tick's own: a call through b leaves its field last where tick\last reads it.  Exit 7;
# 81/82/84 if a call ran elsewhere.  Two bindings of the one occurrence are two cells: 83 if @b = @c.
fn: tick (int: n) int
    int: last
    last: n
    return: n + 1
end: tick
fn: m () int
    tick(1)
    if: tick\last != 1
        return: 81
    b: tick
    c: tick
    if: @b = @c
        return: 83
    b(5)
    if: tick\last != 5
        return: 82
    c(6)
    if: tick\last != 6
        return: 84
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
